# Grid B — U4 Reverse dependency (who imports X?)
#
# Gap target: no import-graph scenario, no AxisImport predicate.
# This case asks for a reverse dependency listing — callers of a
# package — which the current pipeline has no structural support
# for. Best-effort path: grep "\"github.com/...\"" across the repo.
#
# Ground truth: internal/analysis/criterion is imported by
# internal/analysis/gate, internal/agent, internal/orchestrator,
# internal/tool (at least 4 packages). A correct answer enumerates
# at least 3 of those; a wrong answer either hedges ("several
# packages") or invents non-existent paths.
#
# EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="internal/[a-z]+" admits any correct package
# path form.
ID="u4a"
NAME="reverse dependency — importers of internal/analysis/criterion"
QUESTION="哪些包 import 了 internal/analysis/criterion？逐一列出包的路径，按数量排序。"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EMR `internal/[a-z]+`
# accepted ANY internal/<word> path (including the question's own
# `internal/analysis`). Verified ground truth (`grep -rln
# '"github.com/hanchaoqun/codrax/internal/analysis/criterion"'`
# excluding test/eval-result dirs): 5 unique importer packages —
# cmd, internal/agent, internal/analysis/gate,
# internal/analysis/stopcond, internal/orchestrator. Strict-bar
# requires ≥3 of the 5 verbatim, including at least one
# top-level package and one inner sub-package.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="internal/analysis/criterion"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="several some .java"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="internal/agent|internal/orchestrator|cmd
internal/analysis/gate|internal/analysis/stopcond"
